    "title": "USB 3.0 is quietly breaking your Wi-Fi, and Intel warned everyone years ago - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kazim Alvi ,\n21 hours ago USB 3.0 was considered a major performance upgrade over USB 2.0 when it was first introduced around 17 years ago. The USB family has since evolved through USB 3.1, USB 3.2, and USB4, which boast higher transfer speeds, but USB 3.0 remains relevant today, and you can easily find devices that still use the standard. I have got a few USB 3.0 flash drives and a USB hub. As surprising as it may sound, these devices have a problem that directly impacts your router's 2.4GHz Wi-Fi band. It's not limited to that; the problem even affects your mouse and keyboard. Read full article",
